  "name": "Scent ruins",
  "description": "A sunken stone ring in the Plains that still hums with old scent (data/terrain.ts `ruins`): a raised lip of the hive's own grown carapace, lit along its far edge and split in three places, a dark bowl inside it and the signal glowing at the bottom with its light in rings up the bowl — the hive's light, lit from inside. Three standing stones lean round the rim, each lit down its left, seamed, with a lit top edge, the signal in a vein of its seam and the dark of the ground at its foot; chips of them lie where they fell, and lichen has got onto the tallest. Footprint and stones where the old document had them. Generated by scripts/terrain.py.",
